WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.205
Follow one tRNA all the way through.

00:00:02.495 --> 00:00:03.703
It enters at the A site.

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:06.118
Its anticodon matches, so it stays.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.416
A peptide bond forms at the P

00:00:08.567 --> 00:00:08.950
site.

00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:11.029
Then our tRNA moves to the P

00:00:11.179 --> 00:00:11.563
site.

00:00:12.097 --> 00:00:14.094
Another tRNA comes in, and the chain

00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:14.860
is handed over.

00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:17.112
Now our tRNA moves to the E

00:00:17.216 --> 00:00:18.354
site, empty.

00:00:18.691 --> 00:00:19.410
Then it leaves.

00:00:20.037 --> 00:00:22.220
A, then P, then E, like stops

00:00:22.255 --> 00:00:22.986
on a train line.

00:00:23.207 --> 00:00:24.577
Now try the question again.
